From 6616301f95bd842e637160e6029d3b1408877ea9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:07:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] build: require OpenSSL 3.0 and compile against the OpenSSL
 that was found

find_package(OpenSSL 1.1.1) let the node build against an end-of-life
OpenSSL it no longer compiles with. OpenSSL 1.1.1's public sha.h
defines a U64(C) macro, which breaks LogField::U64() in logging/event.h
in every translation unit that includes OpenSSL before logging.h
(httpserver.cpp, net_websocket_tls.cpp).

Require 3.0, the oldest API the TLS code uses (upstream no longer
supports 3.0 either, but Debian 12, Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and RHEL 9 ship
patched 3.0.x as their system OpenSSL). Release builds use depends'
3.5 LTS. The one feature that needs 3.5, the X25519MLKEM768 hybrid key
exchange, is already detected at run time with a fallback to X25519. A
configure warning now says so when OpenSSL is older than 3.5. Raising
the minimum to 3.5 would break building with those distributions'
OpenSSL for no code reason. The planned QUIC transport can require 3.5
for itself when it lands.

Search the found OpenSSL's headers ahead of other dependencies' include
directories. Homebrew links one OpenSSL's headers (now 4.0.3) into
/opt/homebrew/include, which Boost and others add as -isystem before
OpenSSL's own directory. A macOS build pointed at another OpenSSL with
OPENSSL_ROOT_DIR therefore compiled against Homebrew's headers and
linked the other OpenSSL's libraries. Against depends' 1.1.1t that
failed to link (EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_ec_param_enc is a macro in 1.1.1 and a
function in 3.x). Against a same-ABI pair it would have linked silently.
An extra -I cannot fix this: clang drops an -I for a directory that is
also an -isystem.

Evidence (macOS arm64, OPENSSL_ROOT_DIR at depends' 3.5.9 prefix):
- Configure finds 3.5.9.
- Before this change, tls_util.cpp's OpenSSL headers resolved to
  /opt/homebrew/include. After it, all 83 resolve to the depends prefix,
  and no object in the build depends on a Homebrew OpenSSL header.
- bitcoind and test_bitcoin link no OpenSSL dylib and embed "OpenSSL
  3.5.9".
- The base tree against depends' 1.1.1t fails to compile on U64, as
  above.

Not tested: building against a 3.0.x-3.4.x OpenSSL, and Linux or Windows
builds of the node.

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Retain found-header minimum OpenSSL3.0 and SSL_CTX runtime hybrid-group support alongside existing listener code; shared and native builds use one TLS context path.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.
---
 doc/dependencies.md |  5 +++--
 src/CMakeLists.txt  | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/dependencies.md b/doc/dependencies.md
index a71037014a5b6e4540e727249e3cc446694869a8..f502528ce722b3d09437dd202c2c784cb5595389 100644
--- a/doc/dependencies.md
+++ b/doc/dependencies.md
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ These are the dependencies currently used by Bitcoin ABC. You can find instructi
 | libpng |  |  |  |  | Yes |
 | librsvg | |  |  |  |  |
 | Ninja |  | [1.5.1](https://github.com/ninja-build/ninja/releases) |  |  |  |
-| OpenSSL | [3.5.9](https://openssl-library.org/source/) |  | No |  |  |
+| OpenSSL | [3.5.9](https://openssl-library.org/source/) | 3.0 | No |  |  |
 | PCRE |  |  |  |  | Yes |
 | protobuf | [21.12](https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/releases/tag/v21.12) |  | No |  |  |
 | Python (tests) |  | [3.10](https://www.python.org/downloads) |  |  |  |
@@ -39,7 +39,8 @@ factors that affect the dependency list.
 
 #### Options passed to `cmake`
 * Berkeley DB and SQLite are not needed with `-DBUILD_WALLET=OFF`.
-* OpenSSL is not needed with `-DENABLE_BIP70=OFF`.
+* OpenSSL is always needed: the node terminates TLS itself (RPC, `-publicbind`
+  and WebSocket P2P listeners, and `wss://` dialing).
 * protobuf is not needed with `-DENABLE_BIP70=OFF`.
 * Qt is not needed with `-DBUILD_QT=OFF`.
 * qrencode is not needed with `-DENABLE_QRCODE=OFF`.
diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index 1be6bf077551886654150a9abb7c92f6c484ccf6..d41620a016d6f571edd146217f32336cb3ce6966 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -737,7 +737,22 @@ endif()
 # supports zstd content encoding.
 include(BrewHelper)
 find_brew_prefix(OPENSSL_ROOT_DIR openssl)
-find_package(OpenSSL 1.1.1 REQUIRED)
+# OpenSSL 3.0 is the oldest API the TLS code is built for; 1.1.1 is end of
+# life. Release builds use depends' 3.5 LTS. Features that need a newer
+# OpenSSL check for it at run time (the X25519MLKEM768 key exchange needs
+# 3.5).
+find_package(OpenSSL 3.0 REQUIRED)
+if(OPENSSL_VERSION VERSION_LESS 3.5)
+	message(WARNING
+		"OpenSSL ${OPENSSL_VERSION}: the TLS client cannot offer the "
+		"X25519MLKEM768 post-quantum hybrid key exchange (needs OpenSSL 3.5)")
+endif()
+# Search the found OpenSSL's headers before other dependencies' include
+# directories. Homebrew links one OpenSSL's headers into its shared include
+# directory, which other dependencies add, so with OPENSSL_ROOT_DIR pointing
+# elsewhere the build would compile against those headers and link the
+# other OpenSSL's libraries.
+include_directories(BEFORE SYSTEM ${OPENSSL_INCLUDE_DIR})
 find_package(Zstd 1.4.0 REQUIRED)
 target_link_libraries(server OpenSSL::SSL OpenSSL::Crypto Zstd::zstd)
 target_compile_definitions(server PRIVATE HAVE_ZSTD=1)
-- 
